---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Beresin Digital';
const description =
  'Beresin Digital Privacy Policy: what data we collect, how we use it, the third parties that process it, and your rights as a data subject under PDP Law No. 27/2022.';
---

<LegalLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lead="This document explains what personal data we collect through this site, what we use it for, and your rights over that data."
  updated="October 6, 2026"
  locale="en"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy applies to the site <strong>{site.domain}</strong>, operated
    by <strong>{site.legalName}</strong> ("we") as the controller of personal data, domiciled
    in {site.address.city}, {site.address.countryName}. We process personal data in accordance with
    Law No. 27 of 2022 on Personal Data Protection ("PDP Law") and its implementing regulations.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>

  <h3>a. Data you provide yourself</h3>
  <p>
    When you fill in a consultation or contact form, we collect your full name, WhatsApp/phone
    number, email address (optional), and a description of your project needs. We also record which
    page the form was submitted from.
  </p>

  <h3>b. Technical data</h3>
  <p>
    Our server records IP address, device type, and access time for security, abuse prevention, and
    rate limiting. For form submissions, the IP address is stored in
    a <strong>salted hash (HMAC)</strong> form, not the raw address, in line with the principle of
    data minimisation.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Basis and purposes of processing</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Basis for processing</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Responding to consultation and proposal requests</td>
        <td>Your consent; performance of a contract</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Preventing spam, abuse, and security attacks</td>
        <td>Our legitimate interest</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Site visit analytics (aggregate statistics)</td>
        <td>Your consent (analytics cookies)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Compliance with legal and administrative obligations</td>
        <td>Legal obligation</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>We do not use your data for targeted advertising and do not sell personal data.</p>

  <h2>3. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses two different kinds of measurement, and we distinguish them transparently:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — cookieless measurement with no personal
      identification. Data is aggregate (visit counts, popular pages, referrers). Because it does not
      process personal data, this technology does not require consent, but we disclose it here
      anyway.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</strong> — uses cookies and can identify a device. GA4 cookies
      are <strong>only loaded after you give consent</strong> through the banner shown on your first
      visit. If you decline, the GA4 script does not run at all. We also enable Google Consent Mode
      v2 with all initial states set to <em>denied</em>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can change or withdraw your choice at any time via the "Cookie Preferences" link in the
    banner and in the site footer.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third parties that process data</h2>
  <p>
    We use a number of service providers that process data on our behalf under data processing
    agreements:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Role</th>
        <th>Data</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td>
        <td>CDN, security, and web analytics</td>
        <td>Request metadata; aggregate cookieless statistics</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Google (GA4)</td>
        <td>Visit analytics</td>
        <td>Device and interaction data — only after consent</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Brevo (Sendinblue)</td>
        <td>Notification email delivery</td>
        <td>Message contents and destination email address</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>VPS provider in Indonesia</td>
        <td>Database and site file storage</td>
        <td>All application data</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Application data (database and files) is stored on server infrastructure located in Indonesia.
    Cloudflare's CDN terminates TLS at the point nearest to you, so some request metadata may pass
    through Cloudflare infrastructure outside Indonesian territory. We have signed data processing
    agreements with these providers.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Lead data from forms: maximum <strong>24 months</strong> since last contact.</li>
    <li>Security and rate-limit logs: maximum <strong>90 days</strong>.</li>
    <li>Aggregate analytics data: per the provider's retention configuration (maximum 14 months for GA4).</li>
    <li>Contract and administrative documents: per applicable legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Once the retention period ends, data is permanently deleted or anonymised.</p>

  <h2>6. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We apply reasonable technical and organisational measures, including TLS encryption on all site
    traffic, storing administrator passwords with the <strong>argon2id</strong> algorithm,
    restricting access to the admin panel, audit logging, and regular database backups.
    Nevertheless, no method of transmission or storage is entirely free of risk.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights as a data subject</h2>
  <p>Under the PDP Law, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>obtain information about our identity, and the basis and purposes for processing your data;</li>
    <li>access and obtain a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>request updates or corrections to inaccurate data;</li>
    <li>request the deletion of your personal data;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent to data processing;</li>
    <li>object to certain processing;</li>
    <li>request restriction of data processing;</li>
    <li>file a claim and/or receive compensation for violations of your rights.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Requests can be made by email
    to <a href={`mailto:${site.emailProcurement}`}>{site.emailProcurement}</a>. We will verify your
    identity and respond within <strong>3×24 hours</strong> as required by the PDP Law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Minors</h2>
  <p>
    This site is intended for businesses and institutions, not for children under 18. We do not
    knowingly collect children's personal data. If you become aware of any such data, contact us and
    we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest version is always marked with
    the "Last updated" date at the top of the page. Material changes will be communicated via a
    notice on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this Privacy Policy can be sent to:<br />
    <strong>{site.legalName}</strong><br />
    {site.address.city}, {site.address.countryName}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.emailProcurement}`}>{site.emailProcurement}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
